# bench.env.example -- local bench settings for the zz_build_* scripts.
#
# Copy to bench.env (gitignored) and fill in your own values once:
#   cp bench.env.example bench.env
# Every zz_build_* script loads bench.env by itself, so the flash command stays
#   bash ./zz_build_gateway_fbl.sh program
# with nothing to set per terminal. A value already set in the environment
# wins over the file (the := form below only fills in what is unset).

# KitProg3 probe serials, so `program` flashes the right kit with both plugged
# in (F-012). List them with:
#   C:\Infineon\Tools\ModusToolboxProgtools-1.8\fw-loader\bin\fw-loader.exe --device-list
# and match each to its COM port (the serial is the kit's, not the USB socket's).
: "${NODE_A_PROBE:=}"     # Node A, gateway
: "${NODE_B_PROBE:=}"     # Node B, actuator

# Node A app signing key (M4, ADR-0019): the FBL accepts only signed images.
# Relative paths resolve against the repo root. Leave empty for a CRC32 stamp.
: "${FBL_SIGN_KEY:=ec_p256_dev_private.pem}"
